-- title:
--   Integral level-M' functions lie in the j-finite chart algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and let $K$ be an intermediate field of the Laurent series field $L(\!(q)\!)$ over $L$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain equipped with an algebra structure over which $L$ is its fraction field, such that the image of $q$ in $A$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$; assume $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be a nonzero element whose image in $L(\!(q)\!)$ is the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), that is, of $q^{-1}$ times the rational power series `jNumQ`. Let $g \in \mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ satisfy: $g$ lies in [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull M'`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305), the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,(\mathtt{jq})$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $M'$; every coefficient $g_n$ ($n \in \mathbb{Z}$), viewed in $L$, lies in the image of $A$; $g$ is integral over the $\mathbb{Q}$-subalgebra generated by [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157); and the coefficientwise image of $g$ in $L(\!(q)\!)$ lies in $K$. Then this image, as an element of $K$, is integral over the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by $j$, i.e. it belongs to [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142), the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$.
--
--   This is the integrality half of the good-reduction picture for $X_0(M')$ at a prime $q$ not dividing $M'$, in Igusa's form: a level-$M'$ modular function whose $q$-expansion has coefficients in the discrete valuation ring and which is integral over $\mathbb{Q}[j]$ is already integral over $A[j]$, hence a section on the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model. It feeds the cusp-regularity and supersingular-point statements at full level, where such functions must be shown to lie in the local rings of the integral model at closed points of the $j$-finite chart.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_coeffEmb_mem_chartAlgFin_of_forall_coeff_of_isIntegral_adjoin_jq.lean

